WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.990
Revelation is the most misunderstood book in the Bible.

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:16.450
Some use it to predict the end. Many people fear it, because they don't understand it.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.620
But John wrote it to call all Christians to stay loyal.

00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:37.190
John wrote it as a letter to seven churches: ordinary Christians who lived under Rome.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:49.040
Rome looked unbeatable and demanded loyalty. Revelation calls its readers to stay loyal to Jesus instead.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:58.940
Revelation means unveiling. John is shown God's throne, God is in control, and how the world really works.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:06.450
And the one who wins is a lamb, who conquers by giving himself, not by force.

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:16.400
The story ends in a garden city full of light, where God lives with his people.

00:01:21.240 --> 00:01:24.530
This app walks through it, so that you can understand.
